  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want the floating \"+\" button at the bottom of a topic or MP page, and its setting, so that I reply in one tap the way the legacy app lets me.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator, 2026-11-08)\n\n### Legacy behaviour (legacy `master` @ `21173e77`; not in `2440d79`, added after it)\n- Setting **Réglages › Sujets › Bouton +** with three values (`AppSettingsView.swift:106, 481-482`; `Common.swift:243-262`, `AppReplyButtonBehavior`): **Réponse rapide** (default, `quick`), **Répondre comme le forum** (`forum`), **Pas d'icône** (`hidden`).\n- The page shows a floating button at the bottom: icon `plus` for quick reply, `square.and.pencil` for the forum-style reply; no button when `hidden`, and none on an iPhone in landscape (compact height) (`MessagesView.swift:3065, 3180-3196`).\n- Seen by the operator on a device on 2026-11-08, in the legacy app's settings.\n\n### Current SwiftHFR\nNo floating reply button and no such setting (to be confirmed by the implementer with file:line).\n\n### Scope\n- Port the button and the setting with the same three values, key and default, on topics and MPs.\n- Describe \"Répondre comme le forum\" from the legacy code before porting it: never guess what it opens.\n- The per-post menu is a separate item (#594).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- The three values behave as in legacy on iPhone and iPad, light and dark; the setting persists.\n- Tests on the setting and the button's presence per value and size class.\n\n",
